      "output": "{\n  \"choice\": \"within\",\n  \"base_and_horizon\": {\n    \"text\": \"Nintendo guided for consolidated profit attributable to owners of parent of JPY 200,000 million for the fiscal year ending March 31, 2021 (PDF pp. 2, 4). As of the cutoff, my base case is that the full-year actual lands within the question’s inclusive ±2% band.\",\n    \"evidence_ids\": [\"P2\", \"P1\"]\n  },\n  \"causal_driver\": {\n    \"text\": \"Nintendo said production and shipping delays appeared to be easing, but warned that persistent component shortages could disrupt supply (PDF p. 3). Management expected production and sales to meet full-year demand and software to launch as planned (PDF p. 4). My base case is that Nintendo recovers enough delayed Switch sales by year-end, and that planned software releases support earnings, keeping profit attributable to owners near guidance.\",\n    \"evidence_ids\": [\"P5\", \"P4\", \"P1\"]\n  },\n  \"alternative\": {\n    \"text\": \"Lower: If component shortages persist and Nintendo cannot recover lost Switch shipments by fiscal year-end, weaker hardware sales and fewer software purchases from new Switch owners could push profit more than 2% below the JPY 200,000 million guide (PDF pp. 2–4).\",\n    \"evidence_ids\": [\"P2\", \"P5\", \"P1\"]\n  },\n  \"revision_signal\": {\n    \"text\": \"I would switch from within to lower if, before the full-year results, Nintendo cuts its full-year Switch unit-sales forecast and cites ongoing component shortages. A full-year cut would indicate that management no longer expects to make up the missed sales by year-end (PDF pp. 3–4).\",\n    \"evidence_ids\": [\"P5\", \"P4\", \"P1\"]\n  },\n  \"historical_comparison\": {\n    \"text\": \"The May 7 consolidated forecast table shows the JPY 200,000 million guide as 22.7% below the just-reported fiscal year ended March 31, 2020. The JPY 210,842 million figure in the same release is non-consolidated profit and is not the comparable prior-year figure (PDF p. 2).\",\n    \"evidence_ids\": [\"P2\", \"P3\"]\n  }\n}",
